          "title": "You'll want to know: ねぎる",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ねぎる — negiru — \"to haggle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "いちばで ねぎって、やすく かいました。 — ichiba de negitte, yasuku kaimashita — \"I haggled at the market and bought it cheaply.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Polite ねぎります, negirimasu; a godan verb. Past (polite): ははが いちばで ねぎりました。, haha ga ichiba de negirimashita."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ねぎる (negiru) is a native Japanese word (wago), inherited rather than borrowed from Chinese, built from ne, \"price\" and giru, \"cutting\" (from kiru); its kanji were attached later as kun'yomi (JMdict)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
